   "Modules: commoncrawl.seeds (resources/seeds.edn, operator-editable, embedded fallback), commoncrawl.cdx (CDX query + WARC envelope strip, pure/injected), commoncrawl.extract (regex HTML->text fallback), commoncrawl.llm (murakumo-main extraction via the 70-tools/bmc llm-complete-fn convention), commoncrawl.embeddings (murakumo /v1/embeddings client), commoncrawl.identity (CACAO self-mint on org-chainagnostic-cacao + org-ietf-ed25519, both already nbb-proven), commoncrawl.kotobase (web.ingest/web.search XRPC client matching the deployed lexicon+edge auth exactly), commoncrawl.policy (the Governor: seed-scope/exclude/budget hard, confidence soft), commoncrawl.store (MemStore + langchain-store-backed DatomicStore, ledger/dedupe/cursor/lease/budget/tick-log), commoncrawl.operation (the StateGraph), commoncrawl.loop (the durable outer tick loop), commoncrawl.report, commoncrawl.sim (offline demo), commoncrawl.live-http (the ONLY ns doing real IO, deliberately plain .cljs/nbb, never .cljc)"
   "Real bug found and fixed during implementation, not merely a design note: commoncrawl.cdx's first cut picked a capture by 'most recent timestamp' regardless of HTTP status — live-verified against www.sec.gov's real CC-MAIN-2026-25 index, the newest capture was a contentless 301-redirect stub, silently producing a fetch-miss for a domain that in fact had 113 real 200 captures. Fixed via commoncrawl.cdx/latest-response-capture (filters to status 200 before picking newest), with regression tests (test/commoncrawl/cdx_test.cljc) reproducing the exact bug shape"
   "Test evidence (not claimed, run this session): `clojure -M:test` — 90 tests, 187 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. `clojure -M:lint` (clj-kondo) — 0 errors, 0 warnings. A separate nbb smoke test (test/nbb_smoke.cljs) independently proves the entire actor — every .cljc/.cljs namespace, including a REAL Ed25519 CACAO mint+verify round-trip — loads and runs correctly on the nbb runtime (repo-wide runtime priority: nbb ahead of jvm/bb), not only under clojure -M:test"
   "Live E2E verification, real production services, this session: (1) Common Crawl CDX index query against index.commoncrawl.org — real, 113 captures found for https://www.sec.gov/ in CC-MAIN-2026-25; (2) WARC ranged fetch + real gzip decompression against data.commoncrawl.org — real, 223075 characters of page text extracted (title 'SEC.gov | Home'); (3) CACAO self-mint — a real Ed25519 identity + signed CACAO, independently cacao.core/verify-checked; (4) web.ingest against PRODUCTION kotobase.net — real POST, {:ok true :status 200 :datom_count 5}; (5) web.search against PRODUCTION kotobase.net — real POST, confirmed the just-ingested page is now findable (score 10.21, correct url/title/snippet)"
   "NOT live-verified: the :advise LLM-extraction step (murakumo-main) and the /v1/embeddings call. No murakumo bearer token was obtainable non-interactively this session — the kagi vault available to this session did not contain the MURAKUMO_CRITIC_TOKEN item skill secrets-location-map documents (a `kagi pull` was attempted to check for it, found the cloud vault snapshot had FEWER items than local and was immediately restored from `kagi`'s own pre-pull backup rather than accepting the apparent data loss; no push was performed, so cloud state was never altered), and 1Password's `op` CLI was not signed in (interactive auth, which this session correctly did not attempt itself per the safety floor on credential entry). The ingested test page therefore carried no extracted_category/extracted_summary/extracted_entities/embedding fields — all optional/additive per the lexicon, so the ingest itself still succeeded honestly, just without that enrichment. Both legs remain covered only by offline tests (test/commoncrawl/llm_test.cljc, test/commoncrawl/embeddings_test.cljc) and the nbb smoke test's mocked responses — completing live verification of this leg is an explicit open follow-up, not silently marked done"]
