  :adr/body "# ADR-2607192300: kotobase-commoncrawl-actor repo landed\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-19\n**Related**: ADR-2607192200 (the design this repo implements; this ADR records that it was actually built, not just proposed)\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607192200 designed `kotoba-lang/kotobase-commoncrawl-actor` — a seed-domain-list-driven Common Crawl ingestion actor writing into net-kotobase's already-deployed hybrid token+vector `web.ingest`/`web.search` extension — but the design itself did not create the repo. This workspace has a documented failure mode for exactly that gap (the retracted ADR-2607081500 claimed an implemented resident actor that never existed as a repo, west entry, or GitHub repo). This ADR exists to record, with concrete evidence, that this repo was actually implemented, tested, registered, and partially live-verified, not merely designed.\n\n## Decision\n\nSee `:adr/decision` for the full itemized evidence (commit SHA, west registration path, module list, test counts, and an exact accounting of what was and was not live-verified against production Common Crawl / kotobase.net / murakumo). In summary:\n\n- Repo: https://github.com/kotoba-lang/kotobase-commoncrawl-actor (public, `main` @ `5616bc5f2001ba043e640d1beb7ead2da6d7d0a2`).\n- West-registered via the minimal-diff `--entry` path (not a wholesale regeneration), pin-verified server-side.\n- 90 tests / 187 assertions pass under `clojure -M:test`; 0 clj-kondo errors/warnings; a separate nbb smoke test proves the whole actor (including a real CACAO mint/verify round-trip) runs on the nbb runtime.\n- A real bug (picking a capture by 'most recent timestamp' without filtering to HTTP 200, which live-verification against `www.sec.gov` showed can silently pick a contentless redirect stub) was found and fixed during implementation, with a regression test.\n- Live-verified this session against REAL production services: Common Crawl CDX query, WARC ranged fetch + gzip decompression, CACAO self-mint + independent verify, and a real `web.ingest` + `web.search` round-trip against production `kotobase.net`.\n- NOT live-verified: the murakumo LLM-extraction/embeddings leg — no working bearer token was obtainable non-interactively this session (kagi vault lacked the documented item; 1Password required interactive auth this session correctly did not perform). This is an explicit, named follow-up, not glossed over.\n\n## Consequences\n\nSee `:adr/consequences`. In short: a real, auditable artifact exists at the honest scope the parent ADR described, with an explicit, non-hidden gap (LLM/embeddings live verification) left for follow-up."}]
